---
import Shell from '../layouts/Shell.astro';
---
<Shell title="About" page="about">
  <section class="about-page page-wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow instructive-voice">About the feed</p>
    <h1 class="loud-voice">Every word has a story.</h1>
    <p class="story-voice">Explore the origins of English words, save the ones that interest you, and come back whenever curiosity strikes.</p>
    <h2 class="loud-voice">Your data</h2>
    <p class="story-voice">For now, your card stack, liked words, and swipes live only in this browser. This M2 version does not upload swipes or create an account. Clearing this browser’s site data removes your list. Account sync and data deletion controls arrive with the later milestones.</p>
    <h2 class="loud-voice">Sources &amp; credit</h2>
    <p class="story-voice">Word entries come from <a href="https://en.wiktionary.org/">Wiktionary</a>, via <a href="https://kaikki.org/">kaikki.org</a> and the <a href="https://github.com/peterchinman/random-word-generator-site/releases/tag/dictionary-2026-09-20b">Random Word Generator dictionary release</a>. Wiktionary content is available under <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/">CC BY-SA 4.0</a>.</p>
    <p class="story-voice">The server remembers no words served to you yet, so this device keeps its own served list to avoid repeats. The list is stored in IndexedDB alongside your card stack and swipes.</p>
  </section>
</Shell>
